-- Composure Thoughts Extended v4.1.0 ("Readable Thoughts" build).
-- Passive, read-only first-person text presentation for Composure Feedback.
--
-- Architecture change from v2.x: thoughts used to spawn as a single batch
-- (1-5 lines sharing one lifecycle) that had to fully clear before a new
-- batch could appear. v3 replaces that with an independent 5-slot pool:
-- each thought has its own start/fade timeline, a new thought can claim a
-- free slot while others are still on screen, and the headline is just
-- another slot occupant (rendered in caps for emphasis) rather than a
-- permanently reserved 6th slot.
--
-- Additions over v2.0.3:
--   * Slot pool (5 independent thoughts max, not one shared batch).
--   * Claim priority: low-priority triggers (automatic roll, ambient roll,
--     consumable/generic events, escalation) wait for a free slot and are
--     skipped if the pool is full. High-priority triggers (combat contact,
--     entering breaking_point/pass_out) evict the single OLDEST occupied
--     slot to guarantee they're seen.
--   * Ambient roll: a second, independent roll active at High/Medium-High
--     tier ONLY, firing regardless of activity (exploring, mid-firefight,
--     anything) -- weather/Zone/physical-state/mental-want flavor that
--     isn't gated behind being idle.
--   * Valence coloring: any event-sourced thought (consumable, combat,
--     any category) is colored by the sign of the delta that caused it --
--     green for positive, orange for negative -- independent of current
--     tier. A sip of vodka reads calm green even during a breaking_point
--     panic; a combat hit reads alert orange even at full composure.
--     State-driven thoughts (headline, automatic roll, ambient roll,
--     escalation) keep the existing tier-gradient color.
--
-- Text-only presentation effects (jitter, flicker, scramble, ghost/double
-- text) are unchanged in spirit from v2.x but now apply per-slot. No
-- camera or PPE effectors are touched anywhere in this file.
--
-- Every optional dependency (level, level_weathers, IsMonster, framework
-- recovery locks) is pcall-guarded and degrades gracefully if missing.

